  "prefLabel": "Env-A 802.03 Pre-test Notice",
  "priorExpiration": "1999-03-26",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 802.03 Pre-test Notice.\n\n(a) At least 30 days prior to the commencement of source testing, unless a longer period of notification is necessary to comply with a federal testing requirement, the owner or operator shall notify the department of the date(s) of any planned compliance stack testing or RATA testing.\n\n(b) The department shall require the rescheduling of any compliance stack emissions test or RATA if the staff necessary to observe the test is not available.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 800) #5505 eff 11-15-92, EXPIRED: 11-15-98\n\nNew. #6893, INTERIM, eff 11-26-98, EXPIRED: 3-26-99\n\nNew. #7788, eff 10-31-02; ss by #9802, eff 10-31-10; ss by #12762, eff 5-1-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a800.html"
